{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The kept vertices appear in the base’s order at view indices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":". The view keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two arrays, base index to view index and back, so a row is the base’s row filtered and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"renumbered with one array load per entry. A spanning subgraph keeps every vertex at its base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges keep the base’s positions, so a weight closure keyed by the base’s positions works on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the view. An edge is in the view when both its ends are and, if an edge set was given, when it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is in the set. With an edge set the view has dense edge indices, an edge’s index being its rank","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"among the kept edges in base order. Over a base with edge indices the set is a bit mask with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"count per 64-bit word, and a rank costs one popcount. Over a base without them (an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"text":", a complement, an induced subgraph) the set is the sorted kept positions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a row entry or a rank costs a binary search. An induced subgraph has no edge indices, except one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that keeps every vertex, which keeps the base’s rows and edge indices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view holds a copy of the base, so mutating the original doesn’t show through. The base","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must have vertex indices; construction traps when ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexIndexBound","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"As a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GraphAdaptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", its generation is the base’s, and it reads the base’s attached maps.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"[map, of: vertex]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"[map, ofEdgeAt: position]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" trap for a vertex or an edge the view drops,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and their ","type":"text"},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" forms throw. ","type":"text"},{"code":"values(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the base’s, by the base’s positions. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithm on the view reads it only at the kept edges.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/DirectedEdges","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeIndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/EdgeRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/IndexRow","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/UndirectedEdges"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/base"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checked:)-2n5fj","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checked:)-34kf9","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checkedEdgeAt:)-40a5z","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:checkedEdgeAt:)-7lnri","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:of:)-16yvl","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:of:)-3uhp3","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:ofEdgeAt:)-1tfjm","doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/subscript(_:ofEdgeAt:)-8bx4q"],"anchor":"Subscripts","generated":true,"title":"Subscripts"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph-Implementa